        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Leonard Wilson Keenan\r\n\r\nOur Business is you\r\n\r\nDEVELOPMENT OPPORTUNITY\r\n\r\nMulti Unit Property\r\n\r\nRichard Todd of Leonard Wilson Keenan is delighted to present 73 Amiens Street to the Dublin 1 property market.\r\n\r\nSituated on the ever-popular Amiens Street in the heart of Dublin City Centre, this impressive three-storey Georgian mid-terrace property presents a rare opportunity to acquire a substantial period building full of character and exceptional potential. Comprising six generously proportioned bedrooms, three bathrooms and three reception rooms, the property extends over three levels and, while requiring complete refurbishment, retains many of its original Georgian features. Previously divided into apartments and rental accommodation, the property is now fully vacant, offering the incoming purchaser a blank canvas to restore, renovate or redevelop, subject to the necessary planning permissions.\r\n\r\nApproached via granite steps, the attractive Georgian façade immediately creates a striking first impression. Upon entering, the grandeur of the property is evident with its impressive entrance hall featuring soaring double-height ceilings, ornate original plasterwork and elegant period detailing that reflect the craftsmanship of the Georgian era.\r\n\r\nThe flexibility of the layout makes this an ideal opportunity for a variety of purchasers. The property would lend itself to restoration as an elegant period residence, high-quality residential accommodation, continued use as room rental accommodation, or redevelopment as professional offices or consulting rooms, subject to the necessary consents.\r\n\r\nThe location is second to none, occupying a prime position within Dublin City Centre. The International Financial Services Centre (IFSC) is less than a ten-minute walk away, while Connolly Station, offering Irish Rail, DART, Luas Red Line and numerous Dublin Bus services, is just a short stroll from the property. O'Connell Street, Trinity College Dublin, the Docklands and many of Dublin's largest employers are all within comfortable walking distance, making this an exceptionally convenient address for both residential and commercial use. The surrounding area is well served by an excellent selection of cafés, restaurants, shops, supermarkets and leisure facilities, while Dublin Airport is approximately 20 minutes away by car and is easily accessible by public transport.\r\n\r\nOffering an abundance of original character, generous accommodation and an unrivalled city centre location, 73 Amiens Street represents an exceptional opportunity for investors, developers and owner-occupiers alike. Requiring refurbishment but rich in period charm and endless potential, this is a property that offers the chance to create something truly special in one of Dublin's most established and sought-after locations.\r\n\r\n***All information provided is to the best of our knowledge. The utmost of care and attention has been placed on providing factual and correct information. In certain cases some information may have been provided by the vendor to us. We do not hold any responsibility for mistakes, errors or inaccuracies in our online advertising and give each and every viewer the right to get an opinion on any concern they may have***"
      },
